## Summary

This wraps  in a try-catch to gracefully handle the case when the IPC channel is closed during graceful shutdown.

## Problem

Previously,  would throw an unhandled error when the parent process closed the IPC channel while the worker was still attempting to send final status updates (e.g., during job completion).

This caused:
- Worker process crashes without cleanup
- Orphaned worker processes
- Missing final job state notifications
- Harder debugging of job failures

## Solution

Now :
- Catches channel close errors and logs at **debug level** (not error)
- Logs unexpected errors at **error level**
- Returns  when send fails, allowing caller to continue gracefully

## Changes

```typescript
const safeSend = (msg: IPCMessage): boolean => {
  try {
    if (process.connected && process.send) {
      process.send(msg);
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  } catch (error) {
    // Channel closed is expected during graceful shutdown
    if (error instanceof Error && error.message.includes('Channel closed')) {
      log().debug({ msgCase: msg.case }, 'IPC channel closed, message not sent');
    } else {
      log().error({ error, msgCase: msg.case }, 'IPC send failed unexpectedly');
    }
    return false;
  }
};
```

