`/play <playlist_url>` loads the queue but never starts playback — `Creating DisTubeStream` debug message never fires. Individual songs work fine.

**Root cause:** `@distube/ytpl` returns video URLs with playlist context params (e.g. `watch?v=xxx&list=PLyyy&index=3`). When passed to yt-dlp for stream extraction, yt-dlp interprets `&list=` as a playlist request and either hangs fetching metadata for all videos or returns playlist JSON that fails the `isPlaylist()` guard in `getStreamURL`.

**Fix:**

- **`src/utils/helpers.js`** — New `cleanPlaylistParams(url)` utility strips `&list=` and `&index=` params:
  ```js
  function cleanPlaylistParams(url) {
    try {
      const u = new URL(url);
      u.searchParams.delete('list');
      u.searchParams.delete('index');
      return u.toString();
    } catch {
      return url;
    }
  }
  ```
- **`src/index.js`** — `getStreamURL` override now cleans URLs before delegation:
  ```js
  ytPlugin.getStreamURL = async (song) => {
    if (!song.url) throw new Error("No URL found to extract stream");
    return ytdlpPlugin.getStreamURL({ url: cleanPlaylistParams(song.url) });
  };
  ```
- **`patches/@distube+yt-dlp+2.0.1.patch`** — Added `noPlaylist: true` (`--no-playlist`) to `getStreamURL` flags as defense-in-depth
- **`tests/helpers.test.js`** — 7 new tests covering param stripping, passthrough, and invalid URL handling
- **`DEPENDENCIES_AND_FIXES.md`** — Updated technical docs

