The dedupe logic in `DetailsController` was using `!isset()` to drop duplicate `H:i` departure times, but with `ORDER BY departureTime ASC`, the 1900-year bogus record arrives first and gets kept — discarding the correct current-year record.

## Changes

- **`DetailsController::index()`**: Replace `!isset()` check with an explicit datetime comparison, so a later `departureTime` always overwrites an earlier one for the same `routeId + H:i` key.

```php
// Before: first-seen wins (retains 1900-year record)
if (!isset($operationsByRoute[$routeId][$dedupeKey])) {
    $operationsByRoute[$routeId][$dedupeKey] = $operation;
}

// After: newest datetime wins (correct year replaces 1900 record)
$existing = $operationsByRoute[$routeId][$dedupeKey] ?? null;
if ($existing === null || $operation->getDepartureTime() > $existing->getDepartureTime()) {
    $operationsByRoute[$routeId][$dedupeKey] = $operation;
}
```

