Adds a GitHub Actions workflow that enforces issue checklists on close and auto-creates subtask issues for `[extra]` items, plus a reference template documenting the system.

## Workflow (`.github/workflows/subtasks-on-close.yml`)

Triggers on `issues: closed`. Three outcomes based on unchecked checklist items:

- **Required tasks incomplete** → reopen issue + comment listing the blockers
- **All required done, `[extra]` items unchecked** → create a child issue per item + summary comment
- **Negative gate** (`no-subtask-automation` label present) → skip entirely

Checklist item markers:

| Suffix | Effect |
|---|---|
| *(none)* | Required — blocks close |
| `[optional]` / `[cancelled]` | Exempt, ignored |
| `[extra]` | Creates child issue if unchecked |

Example issue body:
```markdown
- [ ] Implement core feature
- [ ] Write unit tests
- [ ] Add benchmarks [extra]
- [ ] Backport to v1 [cancelled]
```

## Reference template (`ISSUE_DRAFT.md`)

New file at repo root documenting marker semantics, opt-out instructions, and an example checklist for issue authors.

