<summary>Original prompt</summary>

Add automation to enforce issue checklist and auto-create "extra" subtasks on close, with a negative gate label to disable the automation.

Changes to make:
1) Add a GitHub Actions workflow at .github/workflows/subtasks-on-close.yml with the following behavior:
   - triggers on issues: closed
   - if the closed issue has the label "no-subtask-automation", do nothing (negative gate)
   - parses the issue body for unchecked checklist items (lines like "- [ ] task text")
   - treats checklist items as exempt if they end with markers: [extra], [optional], or [cancelled]
   - if there are any unchecked REQUIRED tasks (no exempt marker), reopen the issue and post a comment listing the incomplete required tasks
   - if there are unchecked items marked with [extra], create new issues for each and comment with the created list
   - requires issues: write permission
   - configurable: only run when issue contains a specific label (not requested here), but the negative gate label must be respected

   Use actions/github-script@v6 to implement the parsing and API calls. The workflow must check issue.labels for the presence of "no-subtask-automation" and exit early if present.

   Workflow content to add (exact file path: .github/workflows/subtasks-on-close.yml):

   name: Enforce issue checklist & create extra subtasks

   on:
     issues:
       types: [closed]

   permissions:
     issues: write

   jobs:
     handle-issue-close:
       name: Check closed issue for incomplete tasks and handle [extra]
       runs-on: ubuntu-latest
       steps:
         - name: Parse issue body and enforce rules
           uses: actions/github-script@v6
           with:
             script: |
               const issue = context.payload.issue;
               if (!issue) {
                 core.info("No issue in payload — exiting.");
                 return;
               }

               const issueNumber = issue.number;
               const repoOwner = context.repo.owner;
               const repoName = context.repo.repo;
               const body = issue.body || "";

               // Negative gate: if label 'no-subtask-automation' present, exit
               const labels = (issue.labels || []).map(l => (typeof l === 'string') ? l.toLowerCase() : (l.name || '').toLowerCase());
               if (labels.includes('no-subtask-automation')) {
                 core.info("Issue has 'no-subtask-automation' label — skipping automation.");
                 return;
               }

               // Extract checklist lines like "- [ ] task text [extra]"
               const checklistRegex = /^\s*[-*]\s+\[\s\]\s*(.+?)(?:\s*\[(extra|optional|cancelled)\])?\s*$/i;
               const lines = body.split(/\r?\n/);

               const uncheckedNonExempt = [];
               const uncheckedExtra = [];

               for (const line of lines) {
                 const m = line.match(checklistRegex);
                 if (m) {
                   const taskText = m[1].trim();
                   const marker = (m[2] || "").toLowerCase();
                   if (marker === "extra") {
                     uncheckedExtra.push(taskText);
                   } else if (marker === "optional" || marker === "cancelled") {
                     // exempt — do nothing
                   } else {
                     // no exempt marker — treat as required
                     uncheckedNonExempt.push(taskText);
                   }
                 }
               }

               // If there are required incomplete tasks, reopen and comment.
               if (uncheckedNonExempt.length > 0) {
                 const commentBody = [
                   `:warning: This issue was closed but contains ${uncheckedNonExempt.length} incomplete required task(s). The issue will be reopened until these are completed.`,
                   "",
                   "Incomplete required tasks:",
                   ...uncheckedNonExempt.map(t => `- ${t}`),
                   "",
                   "If some of these should be considered optional, cancelled, or extra subtasks, append `[optional]`, `[cancelled]`, or `[extra]` to the checklist item line so the automation will ignore them on close.",
                 ].join("\n");

                 await github.rest.issues.createComment({
                   owner: repoOwner,
                   repo: repoName,
                   issue_number: issueNumber,
                   body: commentBody,
                 });

                 // Reopen the issue
                 await github.rest.issues.update({
                   owner: repoOwner,
                   repo: repoName,
                   issue_number: issueNumber,
                   state: "open",
                 });

                 core.info(`Reopened issue #${issueNumber} because of ${uncheckedNonExempt.length} required incomplete tasks.`);
                 return;
               }

               // All required tasks are complete — create issues for unchecked [extra] item...

</details>



