The snake game leaderboard was `localStorage`-only — every visitor saw only their own browser's scores, and no shared state existed. This replaces it with a live, globally-shared leaderboard backed by the existing Render backend and persisted to the repo via the GitHub Contents API.

## Changes

- **`data/leaderboard.json`** — new file; single source of truth for all scores, committed to the repo by the backend on every submission (`[skip ci]`)
- **`backend/spotify-backend.js`** — adds `GET /api/leaderboard` and `POST /api/leaderboard`
  - Reads/writes `data/leaderboard.json` via GitHub Contents API (survives Render free-tier restarts)
  - 30 s in-memory cache; top-10 cap; score validated as integer in `[1, 10000]`
  - Requires `GITHUB_TOKEN` env var (PAT with `Contents: Read & Write`) on the Render service
- **`js/easter-egg.js`** — `getLeaderboard`, `addToLeaderboard`, `qualifiesForLeaderboard` made `async`, targeting the same Render backend already used for Spotify
  - `showLeaderboardModal` now fetches the live board before render and refreshes it after submission with a "Submitting…" state
  - `particleGameOver` uses `.then()` to handle the async qualification check
  - `localStorage` retained as a silent offline fallback

```js
// Before — per-browser only
function getLeaderboard() {
  return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('snake_leaderboard') || '[]');
}

// After — global, with localStorage fallback
async function getLeaderboard() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch(`${LEADERBOARD_API_BASE}/api/leaderboard`);
    return await res.json();
  } catch {
    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('snake_leaderboard') || '[]');
  }
}
```

## Required setup

Add to the Render service environment before deploying:

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| `GITHUB_TOKEN` | PAT with `Contents: Read & Write` on `indrolend/indrolend-website` |

