Two production bugs on Render: `express-rate-limit` crashes due to untrustred `X-Forwarded-For` headers, and CORS is open to all origins.

## Changes

- **Trust proxy** — adds `app.set('trust proxy', 1)` before rate-limit middleware, required when running behind Render's reverse proxy
- **Restrict CORS** — replaces open `cors()` with an explicit allowlist

```js
// Before
app.use(cors());

// After
app.set('trust proxy', 1);
app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://siddd-is7765.github.io', 'http://localhost:3000'],
  credentials: true
}));
```

