> ## Problem
> 
> The backend deployed on Render has two issues visible in production logs:
> 
> ### 1. `trust proxy` not set — causing `express-rate-limit` to crash
> 
> Render runs behind a reverse proxy, which sends `X-Forwarded-For` headers. The `express-rate-limit` middleware throws this error:
> 
> ```
> ValidationError: The 'X-Forwarded-For' header is set but the Express 'trust proxy' setting is false (default).
> ERR_ERL_UNEXPECTED_X_FORWARDED_FOR
> ```
> 
> **Fix:** Add `app.set('trust proxy', 1);` before the rate limiter middleware in `server/server.js`.
> 
> ### 2. CORS is open to all origins
